; For Audi A3 (8P) - No guaranties
Byte 00 Bit 0 Selective Central Locking (Single door opening)
Byte 00 Bit 1 Central Locking without Safe-Function
Byte 00 Bit 2 Central Locking without sensible Safe-Function
Byte 00 Bit 3 Auto-Lock (automatic locking from 15 km/h)
Byte 00 Bit 4 Auto-Unlock (unlocking after removing key from ignition)
Byte 00 Bit 5 Central Locking with intentional use of Safe-Function
Byte 00 Bit 6 Central Locking Lock/Unlock-Switch RR/RL activates total locking
Byte 00 Bit 7 Unknown					(RR = Rear Right / RL = Rear Left)
Byte 01 Bit 0 Central Locking (Rear) Right Sliding door installed
Byte 01 Bit 1 Central Locking (Rear) Left Sliding door installed
Byte 01 Bit 2 Central Locking (Tailgate) 2-motors Central Lock installed in place of Central Lock motor
Byte 01 Bit 3 Central Locking (Tailgate) inside switch via CAN
Byte 01 Bit 4 Central Locking (Tailgate) Softtouch (direct open/no release)
Byte 01 Bit 5 Central Locking (Tailgate) switch controlled
Byte 01 Bit 6 Central Locking (Back) Central Locking actuator installed instead of Central Locking Motor
Byte 01 Bit 7 Central Locking (Back) Tailgate within Central Locking
Byte 02 Bit 0 Unknown
Byte 02 Bit 1 Central Locking (Tailgate) "Security Lock"
Byte 02 Bit 2 Central Locking (Rear)			1-Motor- instead of 2-Motors-Lock installed
Byte 02 Bit 3 Central Locking (Tailgate) 		1-Motor- instead of 2-Motors-Lock installed
Byte 02 Bit 4 Central Locking (Back) Central Locking actuator rear window switch controlled
Byte 02 Bit 5 Central Locking (Back) Central Locking actuator for rear window installed (Hatch philosophy A-MPV)
Byte 02 Bit 6 Central Locking with Single door opening, driver door additional
Byte 02 Bit 7 Central Locking (Back) Locking for roof compartment lid and Rear lid cover (Hatch philosophy Cabrio)
Byte 03 Bit 0 Comfort function inactive
Byte 03 Bit 1 Comfort function power windows/sunroof via door lock drivers door inactive
Byte 03 Bit 2 Comfort function power windows/sunroof via door lock passengers door inactive
Byte 03 Bit 3 Comfort function power windows/sunroof via door lock rear lid inactive
Byte 03 Bit 4 Comfort function power windows/sunroof via power window switch in drivers door inactive
Byte 03 Bit 5 Comfort function power windows/sunroof via remote control inactive
Byte 03 Bit 6 Comfort function autom. closing
Byte 03 Bit 7 Power windows/sunroof disabled after door opening
Byte 04 Bit 0 Comfort opening power windows via door lock active
Byte 04 Bit 1 Comfort opening power windows via power window switch active
Byte 04 Bit 2 Comfort opening power windows via remote control active
Byte 04 Bit 3 Comfort closing power windows via door lock active
Byte 04 Bit 4 Comfort closing power windows via power window switch active
Byte 04 Bit 5 Comfort closing power windows via remote control active
Byte 04 Bit 6 Comfort function after authorized access only in a limited time
Byte 04 Bit 7 Not relevant/Unused
Byte 05 Bit 0 Comfort opening sunroof via door lock active
Byte 05 Bit 1 Comfort opening sunroof via power window switch active
Byte 05 Bit 2 Comfort opening sunroof via remote control active
Byte 05 Bit 3 Comfort closing sunroof via door lock active
Byte 05 Bit 4 Comfort closing sunroof via power window switch active
Byte 05 Bit 5 Comfort closing sunroof via remote control active
Byte 05 Bit 6 Comfort opening type for sunroof (inactive)	(0 = open	/ 1 = lift)
Byte 05 Bit 7 Unknown
Byte 06 Bit 0 Unlocking Confirmation (Blink) via Door Locks
Byte 06 Bit 1 Unlocking Confirmation (Horn) via Door Locks
Byte 06 Bit 2 Unlocking Confirmation (Blink) via Remote Control
Byte 06 Bit 3 Unlocking Confirmation (Horn) via Remote Control
Byte 06 Bit 4 Not relevant/Unused
Byte 06 Bit 5 Not relevant/Unused
Byte 06 Bit 6 Unknown
Byte 06 Bit 7 Adaptation of Horn Confirmation blocked
Byte 07 Bit 0 Locking Confirmation (Blink) via Door Locks
Byte 07 Bit 1 Locking Confirmation (Horn) via Door Locks
Byte 07 Bit 2 Locking Confirmation (Blink) via Remote Control
Byte 07 Bit 3 Locking Confirmation (Horn) via Remote Control
Byte 07 Bit 4 Not relevant/Unused
Byte 07 Bit 5 Not relevant/Unused
Byte 07 Bit 6 Unknown
Byte 07 Bit 7 Unknown
Byte 08 Bit 0 Remote control inactive
Byte 08 Bit 1 Remote control with "Terminal 15 ON" inactive
Byte 08 Bit 2 Remote control range limitation active
Byte 08 Bit 3 Manual remote control learning/unlearning active
Byte 08 Bit 4 Not relevant/Unused
Byte 08 Bit 5 Not relevant/Unused
Byte 08 Bit 6 Activation Blink Signal (Anti-Theft-Warning System)
Byte 08 Bit 7 Activation Horn Signal (Anti-Theft-Warning System)
Byte 09 Bit 0 Doors	(0 = 2-doors / 1 = 4-doors)
Byte 09 Bit 1 Power windows front installed
Byte 09 Bit 2 Power windows rear installed
Byte 09 Bit 3 Central Locking installed
Byte 09 Bit 4 Model	(0 = Left Hand Drive/ 1 = Right Hand Drive)
Byte 09 Bit 5 Not relevant/Unused
Byte 09 Bit 6 Synchronised mirror adjustment
Byte 09 Bit 7 Mirror lowering with reverse gear (only with Memory Seats)
Byte 10 Bit 0 Anti-theft system deactivated
Byte 10 Bit 1 Anti-theft system disarming only via remote control or immobilizer
Byte 10 Bit 2 DWA scharf bei bewusstem Entsafen/Innenraumüberwachung inaktiv
Byte 10 Bit 3 Anti-theft alarm delay (15 sec) inactive (Thatcham)
Byte 10 Bit 4 Not relevant/Unused
Byte 10 Bit 5 Anti-theft system passive arming
Byte 10 Bit 6 Inclination Sensor installed
Byte 10 Bit 7 Interior Monitoring installed
Byte 11 Bit 0 Not relevant/Unused
Byte 11 Bit 1 Not relevant/Unused
Byte 11 Bit 2 Not relevant/Unused
Byte 11 Bit 3 Not relevant/Unused
Byte 11 Bit 4 Siren installed
Byte 11 Bit 5 Siren Tone type		(0 = frequencey modulated	/  1 = discontinuous)
Byte 11 Bit 6 Alarm Siren type		(0 = 10 Alarms (GB/Irland)	/ 1 = 1 Alarm (RDW))
Byte 11 Bit 7 Adaption channel for Siren configuration blocked
Byte 12 Bit 0 Door open warning light in back installed
Byte 12 Bit 1 Not relevant/Unused
Byte 12 Bit 2 Not relevant/Unused
Byte 12 Bit 3 Not relevant/Unused
Byte 12 Bit 4 Not relevant/Unused
